# Text files are stored with LF and checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# Shell scripts must be LF: a CRLF bash script fails on CI's Linux runner with errors about
# `$'\r'`, and editors and Windows text-mode writes (including a Python script's
# `open(path, "w")`) produce CRLF silently. `eol=lf` makes git normalise them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
